                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #333333;">The Department of State Hospitals-Napa, Personnel Office is recruiting to fill a&nbsp;</span>permanent, full-time<span style="color: #333333;">&nbsp;Senior Personnel Specialist vacancy. Applicants will serve as the expert staff resource responsible for the most difficult and complex personnel and payroll issues. Functions as the lead to Personnel Specialists and assists in the monitoring and review of workload to ensure transactions are completed timely and accurately. Must demonstrate the ability to apply the State laws, departmental and control agency rules and regulations, and collective bargaining agreement provisions pertaining to a variety of personnel transactions in the areas of personnel record keeping, certification, payroll, and personnel documents processing and related personnel transactions functions. A Senior Personnel Specialist advises on&nbsp;benefits and processes personnel documentation into the computer. Important characteristics include punctuality, good attendance, positive attitude and effective verbal and written communication skills. They must also have the ability to work independently and to interpret and use job-related reference material. Computer skills are also desirable.<br /></span></span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br /><strong>Per CalHR the Senior Personnel Specialist position is eligible for an annual payment up to&nbsp;$4,800, payable upon meeting the designated criteria as stated in <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.calhr.ca.gov%2FPay%2520Differentials%2520Library%2FPay_Differential_240.pdf%23search%3Dpersonnel%2520specialist&amp;data=05%7C01%7CTeresita.Oracion%40dsh.ca.gov%7C5329af6223854c0b6f8908db62d4c782%7C807536a6a6b14893a01370509c59ebbb%7C0%7C0%7C638212438281811930%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=Y7UVorwtoHWpQlPu%2BZl56sZhSVvzDodH11a9hDGfvsQ%3D&amp;reserved=0" style="text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #0563c1; text-decoration-line: underline;">Pay Differential 240</span></a></strong></span><strong><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"> .</span></strong></p><p style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><a name="_Hlk92277833" style="box-sizing: border-box; background: #ffffff; color: #1b3c5a; text-decoration: underline; text-align: left; font-family: Arial;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;">This advertisement will run until filled with a cutoff date for review on the 15th of each month.</strong></a><br /> </span></strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">To ensure that your application will be considered for this recruitment the following items are required:</span></p><ul type="disc"><li style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong>You are required to review and meet the minimum qualifications and pass the Senior Personnel Specialist examination, located at <a href="https://calcareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/Exams/ExamBulletin.aspx?ExamControlId=1985">Senior Personnel Specialist</a>&nbsp;exam&nbsp;on the CalCareers web site.</strong></span></li><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Include<strong>&nbsp;&quot;<span style="text-decoration: underline;">SENIOR&nbsp;</span></strong><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PERSONNEL SPECIALIST, JC-466554</span></strong>” in the “JOB TITLE(S)” section of the STD 678 Employment Application.</span></li><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Complete      the STD 678 Employment Application&nbsp;in its entirety. Include d</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">uties performed, supervisor’s name and contact information.&nbsp;<span style="text-decoration: underline;">Incomplete applications will be screened out.</span>&nbsp;</span></li><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Resumes      will not be accepted in lieu of information required&nbsp;on the STD&nbsp;678 Employment Application.</span></li></ul><div><p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"></span></p></div><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26503616&name=SPSDutyStatement2.22.2019.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
